From 344c3542cf64ba6a4ea176cd3c2a398f6cd49fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Szendrei <618011+pocker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:42:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] wintypes: Add DataReader and implement the DataWriter
 write methods.

Add Windows.Storage.Streams.DataReader backed by an IBuffer (FromBuffer),
with all the Read* methods, byte order and string encodings. Stream-based
loading (LoadAsync, CreateDataReader) is left unimplemented.

Fill in the DataWriter methods that were stubs: WriteByte, WriteBuffer,
WriteBoolean, WriteGuid, the integer, float, DateTime and TimeSpan
writers, WriteString, MeasureString, and the ByteOrder and
UnicodeEncoding properties. Both classes default to big endian and UTF-8,
like native.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
